* ================================================================
* sky130_hold.lib
* Sample-and-hold switch architectures on SKY130.
* Include AFTER a library from flow/pdk.py with devices='hold'.
* Sizes in um (the PDK library sets scale = 1u).
*
* Every device carries drain/source diffusion geometry: area w*xd, perimeter 2*(w+xd), with a
* diffusion extension xd = 0.29 um. Without it (ad = as = 0) the SKY130 models fall back to a fixed
* ~10 fA junction leakage per device, independent of size, which hides the real droop floor.
* The basic cells of sky130_cells.lib carry no diffusion geometry; they are used only for timing checks.
*
* The bootstrapped switch (architecture 4) uses a behavioural gate drive and is built in the
* testbench (flow/holdstage.py), with the same geometry.
* ================================================================

.param xd=0.29

* Architecture 1: single NMOS switch.
.subckt NSWG a b en vss wn=1 l=0.15
XMN a en b vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
.ends NSWG

* Architecture 2 (and 5, the charge-locked cell): CMOS transmission gate.
.subckt TGG a b en enb vdd vss wn=1 wp=2 l=0.15
XMN a en b vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
XMP a enb b vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 w={wp} l={l} ad={wp*xd} as={wp*xd} pd={2*(wp+xd)} ps={2*(wp+xd)}
.ends TGG

* Architecture 3: TG with half-size dummy switches on the hold side (charge-injection compensation).
* The dummies turn on as the main switch turns off and absorb about half of its channel charge.
* Dummy widths are clamped at the 0.42 um minimum (so below wn = 0.84 they are not half-size).
.subckt TGD a b en enb vdd vss wn=1 wp=2 l=0.15
XMN a en b vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
XMP a enb b vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 w={wp} l={l} ad={wp*xd} as={wp*xd} pd={2*(wp+xd)} ps={2*(wp+xd)}
XDN b enb b vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 w={max(wn/2, 0.42)} l={l}
+ ad={max(wn/2, 0.42)*xd} as={max(wn/2, 0.42)*xd} pd={2*(max(wn/2, 0.42)+xd)} ps={2*(max(wn/2, 0.42)+xd)}
XDP b en b vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8 w={max(wp/2, 0.42)} l={l}
+ ad={max(wp/2, 0.42)*xd} as={max(wp/2, 0.42)*xd} pd={2*(max(wp/2, 0.42)+xd)} ps={2*(max(wp/2, 0.42)+xd)}
.ends TGD

* Architecture 6: T-switch with thick-oxide 5 V NMOS devices (after Caglar 2025, imec).
* Two series switches; in hold the middle node is shunted to vss, so the DAC line does not
* feed through to the hold node. Gate drive enh/enhb swings 0 to 3.3 V.
.subckt TSW a b enh enhb vss wn=1 l=0.5
XM1 a enh m vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
XM2 m enh b vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
XM3 m enhb vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
.ends TSW

* Pad ESD pair on the hold node: diode to vss (n+/p-well) and to vdd (p+/n-well).
* Area in um^2, perimeter in um (scale = 1u).
.subckt ESD node vdd vss a=100 p=40
D1 vss node sky130_fd_pr__diode_pw2nd_05v5 area={a} pj={p}
D2 node vdd sky130_fd_pr__diode_pd2nw_05v5 area={a} pj={p}
.ends ESD

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- droop mitigations

* TG with a high-V_T PMOS (pfet_01v8_hvt): the plain TG's off PMOS is its dominant leak.
.subckt TGH a b en enb vdd vss wn=1 wp=2 l=0.15
XMN a en b vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
XMP a enb b vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_01v8_hvt w={wp} l={l} ad={wp*xd} as={wp*xd} pd={2*(wp+xd)} ps={2*(wp+xd)}
.ends TGH

* T-switch whose middle node is driven to the held voltage in hold (buffer output on pin buf), so the
* hold-side device sees only the buffer offset across it and its subthreshold leakage nearly vanishes.
* Thick oxide (TSWB, 3.3 V gate drive) and thin oxide (NTB, 1.8 V) versions.
.subckt TSWB a b enh enhb buf vss wn=1 l=0.5
XM1 a enh m vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
XM2 m enh b vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
XM3 m enhb buf vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
.ends TSWB

.subckt NTB a b en enb buf vss wn=1 l=0.15
XM1 a en m vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
XM2 m en b vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
XM3 m enb buf vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
.ends NTB

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- transistor-level buffer

* Five-transistor OTA, thick oxide (g5v0d10v5, 3.3 V supply), PMOS input pair, NMOS mirror load.
* Used in unity gain (out tied to inn) as the middle-node buffer of the T-switch (architecture TSWO,
* replacing the behavioural buffer of TSWB). PMOS inputs keep the 0.3-1.5 V held range inside the
* input common-mode range at 3.3 V. The tail mirrors a shared reference (vbp, one per chip):
* tail current = reference current. Long devices for low offset and low current; the buffer only
* has to hold the middle node against leakage, so its bandwidth does not matter.
.subckt OTA5T inp inn out vdd vbp vss wi=2 li=2 wl=1 ll=4 wt=2 lt=2
XMT tail vbp vdd vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wt} l={lt} ad={wt*xd} as={wt*xd} pd={2*(wt+xd)} ps={2*(wt+xd)}
XM1 x inp tail vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wi} l={li} ad={wi*xd} as={wi*xd} pd={2*(wi+xd)} ps={2*(wi+xd)}
XM2 out inn tail vdd sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wi} l={li} ad={wi*xd} as={wi*xd} pd={2*(wi+xd)} ps={2*(wi+xd)}
XM3 x x vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wl} l={ll} ad={wl*xd} as={wl*xd} pd={2*(wl+xd)} ps={2*(wl+xd)}
XM4 out x vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wl} l={ll} ad={wl*xd} as={wl*xd} pd={2*(wl+xd)} ps={2*(wl+xd)}
.ends OTA5T

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- transistor-level bootstrap

* Architecture BOOTT: bootstrapped NMOS switch, transistor level (replaces the behavioural gate drive
* of BOOT). Thin-oxide main switch XMS; the bootstrap network is thick oxide (g5v0d10v5), because
* its nodes reach V_in + VDD (up to 3.3 V). Clocks: enh = -ud..3.3 V (on phase), enhb = 3.3..0 V with
* break-before-make (off phase, the T-switch shunt clock).
*   off phase: XMT1 charges the top plate t to VDD, XMB1 grounds the bottom plate bb, XMG1 pulls the
*              gate to vneg (-ud: gate underdrive), XMX2 holds x at t so XMT2 is off
*   on phase:  XMX1 pulls x to bb, XMT2 connects t to the gate, XMB2 (gate = g) connects bb to the
*              input: the gate sits at V_in + VDD * C_B / (C_B + C_par), a constant overdrive
* XMG1 sits in an isolated p-well (bulk = vneg, deep n-well assumed) so its source can go below ground.
* Nothing but XMS touches the hold node, so the droop floor is XMS's drain junction, as for BOOT.
.subckt BOOTT a b enh enhb vdd vneg vss wn=1 l=0.15 cb=50f wt=0.42 lt=0.5
XMS a g b vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_01v8 w={wn} l={l} ad={wn*xd} as={wn*xd} pd={2*(wn+xd)} ps={2*(wn+xd)}
CB t bb {cb}
XMB1 bb enhb vss vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wt} l={lt} ad={wt*xd} as={wt*xd} pd={2*(wt+xd)} ps={2*(wt+xd)}
XMT1 t enh vdd t sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wt} l={lt} ad={wt*xd} as={wt*xd} pd={2*(wt+xd)} ps={2*(wt+xd)}
XMG1 g enhb vneg vneg sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wt} l={lt} ad={wt*xd} as={wt*xd} pd={2*(wt+xd)} ps={2*(wt+xd)}
XMB2 bb g a vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={2*wt} l={lt} ad={2*wt*xd} as={2*wt*xd} pd={2*(2*wt+xd)} ps={2*(2*wt+xd)}
XMT2 g x t t sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 w={2*wt} l={lt} ad={2*wt*xd} as={2*wt*xd} pd={2*(2*wt+xd)} ps={2*(2*wt+xd)}
XMX1 x enh bb vss sky130_fd_pr__nfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wt} l={lt} ad={wt*xd} as={wt*xd} pd={2*(wt+xd)} ps={2*(wt+xd)}
XMX2 x enh t t sky130_fd_pr__pfet_g5v0d10v5 w={wt} l={lt} ad={wt*xd} as={wt*xd} pd={2*(wt+xd)} ps={2*(wt+xd)}
.ends BOOTT
